## Actual source operands

`prepare_ctf_construction_report` borrows a returned
`ConstructionCtfPublicInitialization` row and the same compiled model. It keeps
the original declared counter separately from ConstructionId, original unmerged
outside-to-inside material order, public count/dt/U/coefficient buffers, selected
surface absorptances and roughness. It invokes no CTF or material arithmetic.
The caller must retain the real model/public generation and used-row selection.

Regular Material uses the actual original JSON/IDF key spelling in Native Name.
NoMass, AirGap and ordinary Construction use uppercase getObjectItem names.
NormalizedName loses this distinction. The four successful compiler loaders now
retain those actual names by original typed ID in `CtfReportNames`. No derived
F/C construction or unsupported material name is invented. Existing coefficient
generation, object counts, material values and declaration order are unchanged.

NoMass's Thickness/Conductivity/Density/SpecHeat report as the four actual
positive-zero MaterialBase defaults. Its stored Resistance is copied. Regular
copies its five actual stored members, including loader Resistance; AirGap uses
the distinct air-material row and stored Resistance. Original layer IDs are used
directly, without merging, recomputing R, or consulting output files.

## Table owner and output sink

`PredefinedStringTable` retains actual allocation, occupied count, declared size
and all eight members of every allocated TableEntryType slot. The unallocated
branch allocates 100 and replaces both counters. The allocated branch increments
and doubles only when required. A string entry then assigns only charEntry,
objectName and indexColumn; untouched members and unused slots remain retained.

`report_ctf_layers` uses supplied genuine pdchOpqConsLayCol column IDs. An empty
column vector returns without writes, as Native does. This unit does not invent
a registry or port the entire SetPredefinedTables catalog. A later ordinary
caller needs its real initialized registry and allocation/counter owners. The
selected Native catalog has ten layer columns; a missing column is a typed Rust
representation boundary after any already written prefix, not a new Native
guard or certification of its unchecked access.

`write_ctf_report_headers` writes the four literal Init headers. Then
`report_ctf_transfer_function` writes the actual construction row, original
material rows and descending NumCTFTerms through zero. The zero row omits Flux.
The selected no-internal-source boundary excludes the source/user QTF suffix.
Counts outside fixed19 are explicit unavailable; no clipping or guessed output.

The EIO sink is a caller-owned `std::io::Write`. Each real row writes immediately;
there is no report buffer hidden inside an error. Actual writer errors return
`CtfReportError::Io` while preserving the already written sink prefix. Typed
scope/owner errors remain separate. Native stream failure/SQLite/callback/global
fatal behavior is not inferred from these Rust sink errors.

## Formatting and verification requirements

Native IOFiles applies its custom rounding only to R/T formats. These report
helpers use ordinary fmt8 F/G. The local formatter retains fixed widths, uppercase
INF/NAN and exponent E, sign bits including negative zero/NaN, significant digits,
rounded-exponent G notation choice and trailing-zero removal. It rounds once via
Rust's standard decimal formatter, then changes decimal text layout only.
No floating rescaling, tolerance, coefficient recomputation or expected array is
introduced. Actual same-input Native byte comparisons across finite boundaries,
ties/carry, large/subnormal values and nonfinite signs remain required before
claiming formatter equivalence.

Eight proposed tests cover formatting boundaries, table allocation/doubling and
retained members, empty/real/missing columns, NoMass defaults/name absence,
descending EIO rows/zero omission, fixed19 capacity, actual writer prefix failure,
and the genuine compiler loader name rules. Test values are explicit report
inputs or formatting literals, never Native endpoint observations. No tests ran.

